 "summary": "No. On BTC, ETH and SOL, price after a SAR flip in either direction moved like price after random candles on 1h, 4h and daily. The same held while price stayed on one side of the SAR. The closest thing to a result is the short after price crossed down the SAR on 1h: price fell 0.07% more than after random candles, but only at 20 candles.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Going long on a flip up (price crosses up the SAR)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "No better than random entries on 1h, 4h or daily, with the default SAR or the slower Start 0.01, Increment 0.01."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting a flip down (price crosses down the SAR)",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "On 1h, price fell 0.07% more than after random candles, just above the luck band. The result shows at 20 candles only. On 4h and daily it showed nothing."
  },
  {
   "use": "Staying in while price is above or below the SAR",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Inside the luck band on every timeframe, long above the SAR and short below it."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, price crossing up the SAR gave 6,663 entries in 4,071 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.06% ahead of random entries, inside a luck band that reaches 0.07%. On 4h the flip fires about a quarter as often and lands at -0.01%. On daily it lands at 0.37%, against a band from -1.68% to 1.68%.",
  "The short after price crossed down the SAR on 1h came in 0.07% better than random, above a band that tops out at 0.05%. It holds without its strongest stretch, signals on Jan 10, 2021. At 10, 50 and 100 candles it is chance. On 4h (-0.18%) and daily (-1.53%) the same short sits inside the band.",
  "The 1h results come from downtrends only. The short on a flip down beat random by 0.10% in downtrends, and its strongest stretch was Nov 7–8, 2022, during the FTX collapse. It still holds without that stretch, but only at 20 candles. In uptrends it showed nothing (0.03%). The long on a flip up showed 0.08% in downtrends but vanishes without signals on Nov 9–10, 2022. In uptrends it showed nothing.",
  "On daily, price above the SAR beat random by 1.98% in uptrends. A run of 183 entries between Feb 27, 2021 and Jan 18, 2022 produces that gap, and without it the result is chance. In downtrends it showed nothing (-1.03%). The daily short below the SAR shows the same pattern: 2.56% in uptrends, from 49 entries between Nov 10, 2021 and Jan 19, 2022. Without those entries it is also chance.",
  "Holding while price is above the SAR on 1h enters on every candle it holds: 82,394 entries in 1,002 separate moves. It ends at 0.01% against random, so the extra entries added no information. The slower SAR (Start 0.01, Increment 0.01) flips about three fifths as often as the default on 1h. Pooled, it shows nothing (0.05%). On SOL alone it beat random by 0.24%, against a band reaching 0.2%. That SOL result holds without its strongest stretch and at 50 and 100 candles, but not at 10. On BTC (-0.07%) and ETH (-0.04%) the same setting showed nothing.",
  "A SAR flip did not time entries on these pairs, so a long bot's take profit and DCA orders carry the deal, not the flip. If you use the SAR, use it as a trend filter beside other start conditions. You can also leave it out of entries. The 1h short on a flip down is a thin lead, and it disappears in uptrends. Test it on your own pair against your bot's take profit before relying on it."
 ],
